# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decode tiers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tier 1 (default) lets playbin pick the highest-ranked decoder and feeds
# kmssink straight from its DMA-BUFs: zero copy, no CPU conversion. On this
# board that is the HEVC/AV1/MPEG-2/VP8 path.
#
# Tier 2 is built only if tier 1 fails: the same file is reopened with
# force-sw-decoders on uridecodebin and a videoconvert in front of kmssink.
# The hardware H.264 decoder (v4l2codecs) cannot negotiate DMABuf caps with
# kmssink on this kernel, so H.264 lands here and is decoded on the CPU.
#
# A tier 1 that never reaches PLAYING is treated as a failure too: some broken
# decoders stall instead of posting an error. The watchdog below gives tier 1
# this many seconds to start before falling back.
#
# Test hook: KMS_PLAY_TIER_WATCHDOG_MS shortens that delay so the fallback path
# can be exercised against a file that really stalls. Never set in normal use.
